Algorithms (no third-party code copied)
=======================================

core/rng.js uses the public-domain algorithms sfc32 (Chris Doty-Humphrey,
PractRand), splitmix32 and the MurmurHash3 mixing steps (Austin Appleby),
written out in the project's own code. core/seal.js uses a CRC-15 check.

Development tools (not shipped, only in package.json devDependencies)
=====================================================================

- terser (BSD-2-Clause) - minifies JavaScript for tools/build-play
- acorn (MIT) - checks in tests/ that the JavaScript is ES2015
- jsQR (Apache-2.0) - reads the game's own QR codes back in tests/, to
  check them with a decoder that was not written for this game
- their dependencies: @jridgewell/* (MIT), buffer-from (MIT),
  commander (MIT), source-map (BSD-3-Clause), source-map-support (MIT)
- fontTools (MIT), Python, only for tools/wordmark.py and
  tools/make-logos.py
- Playwright and Chromium (Apache-2.0 / BSD), pre-installed, only for
  the browser tests and screenshots
